.PP
Tmux needs a terminator key after entering a sub\-table, so the
context\-aware no\-slot variant is realized as
\f[CR]<prefix> H Enter\f[R] here.
A layout\[cq]s slot toggles all its members as a group; a member\[cq]s
slot toggles just that member.
Hiding a layout member parks it in the hidden session but keeps its
\f[CR]lay\f[R] field; re\-showing the layout brings it back.
.SS LAYOUT FAMILY [em] \f[CR]t l ...\f[R]
Borrowing a layout is covered by \f[CR]t b\f[R]: the no\-name chooser
shows all utilities \f[B]and\f[R] layouts, so picking a layout there
borrows all its members.
The layout family itself is just file management.
.PP
