.SS THE BINDINGS FILE
Below is the shape of \f[CR]tum\-bindings.conf\f[R].
The shipped file is this, validated; edit it in place to remap.
.IP
.EX
# tmux\-borrow key bindings \-\- edit this file to remap keys.

# 1. Flip\-flop: bound directly to H in the prefix table,
#    and again under the t leader so it works from either entry path.
bind\-key \-T prefix H switch\-client \-T tum\-flip
bind\-key \-T tum\-root H switch\-client \-T tum\-flip

# 2. The leader: <prefix> t  \->  enter the tum\-root key\-table.
bind\-key \-T prefix t switch\-client \-T tum\-root

# 3. Leaves fire and return to the root table.
#    Interactive bindings run in a popup (they need a TTY for the chooser);
#    non\-interactive bindings use run\-shell.
bind\-key \-T tum\-root b \[rs]
    display\-popup \-E \-w 80% \-h 80% \[aq]tum borrow\[aq] \[rs];\[rs]
    switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-root B \[rs]
    display\-popup \-E \-w 80% \-h 80% \[aq]tum new\[aq] \[rs];\[rs]
    switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-root x \[rs]
    run\-shell \-b \[aq]tum close\[aq] \[rs];\[rs]
    switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-root p \[rs]
    run\-shell \-b \[aq]tum push\[aq] \[rs];\[rs]
    switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-root P \[rs]
    run\-shell \-b \[aq]tum pop\[aq] \[rs];\[rs]
    switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-root i \[rs]
    run\-shell \-b \[aq]tum import\[aq] \[rs];\[rs]
    switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-root I \[rs]
    display\-popup \-E \[aq]read \-p \[dq]utility name: \[dq] name && tum import \[dq]$name\[dq]\[aq] \[rs];\[rs]
    switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-root u \[rs]
    display\-popup \-E \-w 80% \-h 80% \[aq]tum popup\[aq] \[rs];\[rs]
    switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-root ? \[rs]
    display\-popup \-E \[aq]tum cheatsheet\[aq] \[rs];\[rs]
    switch\-client \-T root

# 4. Flip\-flop sub\-table: slot key, focused, chooser, cancel.
bind\-key \-T tum\-flip Enter  run\-shell \-b \[aq]tum flip\[aq]      \[rs];  switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-flip 1      run\-shell \-b \[aq]tum flip 1\[aq]    \[rs];  switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-flip 2      run\-shell \-b \[aq]tum flip 2\[aq]    \[rs];  switch\-client \-T root
# ... one binding per slot key in use ...
bind\-key \-T tum\-flip q      switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-flip Escape switch\-client \-T root

# 5. Group leaders drop into a sub\-table for one more key.
bind\-key \-T tum\-root l switch\-client \-T tum\-layout
bind\-key \-T tum\-root g switch\-client \-T tum\-go
bind\-key \-T tum\-root c switch\-client \-T tum\-config

# 6. Sub\-tables: layout, go, config.
bind\-key \-T tum\-layout e display\-popup \-E \[aq]tum\-chooser \[dq]Edit layout\[dq] <(ls \[ti]/.config/tum/*.layout) /tmp/tum.out && ${EDITOR:\-vi} \[ti]/.config/tum/$(basename \[dq]$(cat /tmp/tum.out)\[dq])\[aq] \[rs]; switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-layout l run\-shell \-b \[aq]ls \[ti]/.config/tum/*.layout\[aq] \[rs]; switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-layout q       switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-layout Escape  switch\-client \-T root

bind\-key \-T tum\-go l run\-shell \-b \[aq]tum ls\[aq]     \[rs]; switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-go c run\-shell \-b \[aq]tum check\[aq]  \[rs]; switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-go s run\-shell \-b \[aq]tum status\[aq] \[rs]; switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-go q       switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-go Escape  switch\-client \-T root

bind\-key \-T tum\-config e run\-shell \-b \[aq]${EDITOR:\-vi} \[ti]/.config/tum/\[aq] \[rs]; switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-config s run\-shell \-b \[aq]tmux show\-options \-g | command grep \[dq]\[at]tum\[dq]\[aq] \[rs]; switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-config q       switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-config Escape  switch\-client \-T root

# 7. Cancel from the leader.
bind\-key \-T tum\-root q       switch\-client \-T root
bind\-key \-T tum\-root Escape  switch\-client \-T root
.EE
.PP
Two implementation notes worth knowing:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Popup vs.\ \f[CB]run\-shell\f[B].\f[R] Any binding that opens the
chooser or prompts needs a TTY, so it runs inside
\f[CR]display\-popup \-E\f[R].
Bindings that are genuinely non\-interactive (push, pop,
close\-when\-unambiguous) use \f[CR]run\-shell \-b\f[R] and skip the
popup.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Result feedback.\f[R] For silent \f[CR]run\-shell\f[R] bindings,
the file can add a \f[CR]display\-message\f[R] on success/failure so a
failed \f[CR]t x\f[R] does not fail invisibly.
.SS NO\-PREFIX ENTRY
You do not have to press the tmux prefix to reach the grouped verbs.
The mechanism is tmux\[cq]s \f[CR]root\f[R] key\-table (the
\f[CR]\-n\f[R] flag = \[lq]no prefix\[rq]): bind one key there to switch
into \f[CR]tum\-root\f[R], and every grouped key works unchanged.
.IP
.EX
# Press F12 anywhere \-> you\[aq]re in tum mode. No C\-b needed.
bind\-key \-n F12 switch\-client \-T tum\-root
.EE
.PP
The \f[CR]<prefix> t\f[R] path and the no\-prefix path can
\f[B]coexist\f[R] [em] both reach the same \f[CR]tum\-root\f[R] table.
The only real constraint is the key choice, because \f[CR]\-n\f[R]
bindings fire in \f[I]every\f[R] pane (shells, vim, emacs, pagers).
.PP
.TS
